**The 3 Logical Operators:**

**1. Logical AND (&&) - Both must be true**

**Truth Table:**
```
A     B     A && B
true  true  true
true  false false
false true  false
false false false
```

**Examples:**
```java
int age = 25;
boolean hasLicense = true;

// Both conditions must be true
boolean canDrive = (age >= 18) && hasLicense;  // true

boolean result1 = true && true;    // true
boolean result2 = true && false;   // false
boolean result3 = false && true;   // false
boolean result4 = false && false;  // false
```

**2. Logical OR (||) - At least one must be true**

**Truth Table:**
```
A     B     A || B
true  true  true
true  false true
false true  true
false false false
```

**Examples:**
```java
boolean isWeekend = true;
boolean isHoliday = false;

// At least one condition must be true
boolean canRelax = isWeekend || isHoliday;  // true

boolean result1 = true || true;    // true
boolean result2 = true || false;   // true
boolean result3 = false || true;   // true
boolean result4 = false || false;  // false
```

**3. Logical NOT (!) - Inverts boolean value**

**Truth Table:**
```
A     !A
true  false
false true
```

**Examples:**
```java
boolean isRaining = false;
boolean isSunny = !isRaining;  // true

boolean result1 = !true;   // false
boolean result2 = !false;  // true
boolean result3 = !!true;  // true (double negation)
```

**Short-Circuit Evaluation:**

**AND (&&) - Stops if first is false:**
```java
int x = 5;
int y = 0;

// Safe! Doesn't divide by zero
if (y != 0 && x / y > 2) {  // y != 0 is false, second part not evaluated
    System.out.println("This won't execute");
}

// Without short-circuit (using &)
if (y != 0 & x / y > 2) {  // CRASH! Evaluates x/y even when y=0
    System.out.println("This crashes");
}
```

**OR (||) - Stops if first is true:**
```java
int x = 10;
int y = 0;

// Safe! Doesn't divide by zero
if (x > 0 || x / y > 2) {  // x > 0 is true, second part not evaluated
    System.out.println("This executes safely");
}
```

**Complex Conditions:**
```java
int age = 25;
double salary = 50000;
boolean hasExperience = true;

// Combining conditions
boolean isEligible = ((age > 21) && (salary > 40000)) || hasExperience;
//                    (true && true) || true
//                         true || true
//                            true

// Working age check
boolean isWorkingAge = (age >= 18) && (age <= 65);

// Multiple conditions
boolean canApply = (age >= 18) && (hasExperience || salary > 30000);
```

**Common Mistakes:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - Using OR when AND is needed
int age = 25;
if (age >= 18 || age <= 65) { }  // Always true!

// ✅ CORRECT - Use AND for range
if (age >= 18 && age <= 65) { }  // Correct range check

// ❌ WRONG - Using & instead of &&
if (x != 0 & 10 / x > 2) { }  // No short-circuit! May crash

// ✅ CORRECT - Use && for short-circuit
if (x != 0 && 10 / x > 2) { }  // Safe with short-circuit

// ❌ WRONG - Double negation (confusing)
if (!!isValid) { }

// ✅ CORRECT - Use directly
if (isValid) { }
```

**Operator Comparison:**

| Operator | Name | Short-Circuit | Use Case |
|----------|------|---------------|----------|
| && | Logical AND | Yes | Conditions that might crash |
| & | Bitwise AND | No | Bit operations |
| \|\| | Logical OR | Yes | Alternative conditions |
| \| | Bitwise OR | No | Bit operations |
| ! | Logical NOT | N/A | Invert boolean |

code:
public class LogicalDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int age = 25;
        boolean hasLicense = true;

        // AND - both must be true
        if (age >= 18 && hasLicense) {
            System.out.println("Can drive");
        }

        // OR - at least one true
        boolean isWeekend = true;
        if (isWeekend || age < 18) {
            System.out.println("No work today");
        }

        // NOT - invert
        boolean isWorking = !isWeekend;
        System.out.println("Working: " + isWorking);

        // Short-circuit prevents crash
        int x = 0;
        if (x != 0 && 10 / x > 2) {  // Safe!
            System.out.println("Won't execute");
        }
    }
}

