**Simple Assignment (=):**
```java
int x = 10;
int y = x;  // y gets value of x
```

**Compound Assignment Operators:**

| Operator | Example | Equivalent To | Result |
|----------|---------|---------------|--------|
| += | x += 5 | x = x + 5 | Adds 5 to x |
| -= | x -= 5 | x = x - 5 | Subtracts 5 from x |
| *= | x *= 5 | x = x * 5 | Multiplies x by 5 |
| /= | x /= 5 | x = x / 5 | Divides x by 5 |
| %= | x %= 5 | x = x % 5 | x modulo 5 |

**Complete Examples:**
```java
int x = 10;

x += 5;  // x = x + 5 → x = 15
System.out.println(x);  // 15

x -= 3;  // x = x - 3 → x = 12
System.out.println(x);  // 12

x *= 2;  // x = x * 2 → x = 24
System.out.println(x);  // 24

x /= 4;  // x = x / 4 → x = 6
System.out.println(x);  // 6

x %= 4;  // x = x % 4 → x = 2
System.out.println(x);  // 2
```

**Key Difference - Implicit Casting:**

```java
// WRONG - Regular operation
byte b = 10;
b = b + 5;  // ERROR! Result is int, cannot assign to byte

// CORRECT - Compound assignment
byte b = 10;
b += 5;  // OK! Compound assignment includes automatic cast
System.out.println(b);  // 15
```

**Why This Matters:**
```java
// Regular operation - explicit cast needed
byte b1 = 10;
b1 = (byte)(b1 + 5);  // Must cast explicitly

// Compound assignment - automatic cast
byte b2 = 10;
b2 += 5;  // Automatic cast included

// Both achieve same result, but += is cleaner
```

**String Concatenation:**
```java
String text = "Hello";
text += " World";  // text = text + " World"
System.out.println(text);  // "Hello World"

text += "!";  // text = text + "!"
System.out.println(text);  // "Hello World!"
```

**Multiple Operations:**
```java
int count = 100;
count += 10;  // 110
count -= 5;   // 105
count *= 2;   // 210
count /= 3;   // 70
count %= 8;   // 6
System.out.println(count);  // 6
```

**Common Mistakes:**

```java
// ❌ MISTAKE 1: Typo - Space in operator
int x = 10;
x =+ 5;  // NOT x += 5! This is x = +5 (assigns 5)
System.out.println(x);  // 5 (not 15!)

// ✅ CORRECT:
x += 5;  // x = x + 5

// ❌ MISTAKE 2: Confusing = with ==
int score = 100;
if (score = 90) { }  // ERROR! Assignment in condition

// ✅ CORRECT:
if (score == 90) { }  // Comparison

// ❌ MISTAKE 3: Not understanding implicit cast
byte b = 10;
b = b + 5;  // ERROR!

// ✅ CORRECT:
b += 5;  // Works with automatic cast
```

**Real-World Examples:**

```java
// Accumulating total
int total = 0;
total += 10;  // Add 10
total += 20;  // Add 20
total += 30;  // Add 30
System.out.println(total);  // 60

// Updating score
int score = 100;
score -= 5;   // Penalty
score += 20;  // Bonus
System.out.println(score);  // 115

// Halving a value
int value = 100;
value /= 2;   // value = 50

// Building strings
String message = "Error: ";
message += "File not found ";
message += "at line 42";
System.out.println(message);
// "Error: File not found at line 42"
```

**Benefits:**
- Shorter, cleaner code
- Automatic type casting for narrow types
- Less repetition
- Fewer typing errors

